# Splitbook conventions

Read `AGENTS.md` first: it points at the docs, ADRs and gotchas for each area. Review rules live in `CODING_STANDARDS.md`, and domain terms in `GLOSSARY.md`.

## Web API (`apps/web`)

- A route handler authenticates with `getAuthUser()`, validates with a Zod schema from `@splitbook/shared/validators/*`, calls a module in `src/lib/services/`, and answers through the helpers in `src/lib/utils/api-response.ts` (`{ data }` on success, `{ error, code }` on failure).
- Mongoose models live in `src/lib/models/`; the path alias `@/*` maps to `apps/web/src/*`.
- Client reads use SWR; shared read hooks live in `src/lib/hooks/`.

## Data model

- An Expense is soft-deleted (`isDeleted`), and it keeps its Tag by stable `tagId` beside the Tag's name.
- A Group embeds its Tags as subdocuments.
- Pure domain logic (money, splits, dates, decoders) lives in `@splitbook/shared`, imported by subpath, so web and Android compute it the same way.
